Title: The Standard Measure
Credit: Written by
Author: A. Screenwriter
Draft date: 6 September 2026

# ACT ONE

= Our hero learns that action paragraphs are exactly sixty columns wide.

INT. NEWSROOM - NIGHT

The bullpen is empty except for one desk lamp. MAYA CHEN, 30s, sits behind a monitor that has not been turned off in four days. She types, stops, deletes the line, and types it again.

A phone buzzes against the desk. She ignores it. It buzzes again.

MAYA
(not looking up)
Whatever it is, the answer is no.

The buzzing stops. A beat. Then the office door opens.

DANNY (O.S.)
It's me.

MAYA
Then the answer is *definitely* no.

DANNY enters, coat still wet, holding two coffees like a peace offering.

DANNY
I brought bribes. And an apology, and a theory about why the mayor's office called the publisher at eleven at night to talk about a story that officially does not exist yet.

MAYA
(taking one)
You brought lukewarm bribes.

CUT TO:

EXT. PARKING GARAGE - CONTINUOUS

Fluorescent light, concrete, and the sound of a car alarm somewhere below. They walk between the pillars, coffees in hand, saying nothing for a while.

DANNY
They killed the story.

MAYA
I know.

DANNY
And you're going to run it anyway.

MAYA ^
Obviously.

.THE ROOF - LATER

A forced scene heading, because the line does not start with INT or EXT.

> THE END <

FADE OUT.
